## Root Cause Hypothesis

1. **[HIGH LIKELIHOOD]** npm test failing due to syntax errors or issues in new .sh files or test files that prevent the test harness from loading/running. The agent claims "All 29 new tests passing" but npm test exit code 3 contradicts this, suggesting the agent didn't actually verify npm test output.

2. **[MEDIUM LIKELIHOOD]** package.json modification broke the test setup (VERSION bump or test suite registration has an issue). The git diff shows package.json changed, which could affect how tests are discovered/run.

3. **[MEDIUM LIKELIHOOD]** Incomplete patrol integration. The plan explicitly lists Task 10: "Fix patrol scanner skip + add `patrol_meta_platform_hygiene()` to `patrol_meta_run`" but the agent's summary doesn't mention integrating with patrol, only that the agent script was created.

